/*
 * Expected log errors for pov.testlist.
 *
 * Each active line is a Python regular expression matched against the
 * complete log line.  Keep rules specific so that unrelated errors still fail.
 */

// Example (disabled):
// arm 0: state: ERROR -> WAIT_MOTOR

// MAVLink heartbeat reports a zero-valued error counter during normal operation.
MAVLink: .*HEARTBEAT.*errors[=:]0\b
\bstatus[=:]\d+\s+uptime[=:]\d+\s+errors[=:]0\b
\berrors[=:]0\b
\berrors[=:]00x[0-9a-fA-F]+\b
\berrors[=:]0w=0\b

// Negative multi-arm scenarios deliberately force a link transaction to time
// out, then verify atomic rejection and a clean retry.
ring: task \d+ timed out waiting for (ACK/ERROR|result \d+)
ring: ERROR seq=\d+
(?i)\[pr_debug\] MAVLink: rotor-ring-(cw|ccw): RING_ERROR seq:\d+, node:\d+ from:\d+->\d+ code:\d+
(?i)\[pr_debug\] MAVLink: RING_ERROR seq=\d+ node=\d+ link=\d+->\d+ code=\d+

// Firmware fault scenarios expect bootloader to reject the staged image or
// simulated flash operation before retrying the same update successfully.
bootloader: (CRC32 mismatch|Flash: erase failed|Flash: write failed|Verify: flash_read failed)
bootloader: (Flashing firmware failed|Staged update rejected)\b
bootloader: Flash verification failed, waiting for retry\.\.\.
bootloader: state: (VERIFY|FLASH) -> ERROR
bootloader: Max retries reached \(3\), aborting
bootloader: Bootloader failed with ret=-5

// Active-transfer cancellation and injected read-only/storage failures are
// successful negative tests; paths are restricted to per-arm test fixtures.
(Sender |Receiver )?Cancelled\b
'0:/pov_arm\d+/[^']+': failed to (send|receive)
cannot open 0:/pov_arm\d+/
lsz: skipped: 0:/pov_arm\d+/firmware/ring-firmware\.bin
lsz: skipped: 0:/pov_arm\d+/layer[0-3]/[^/]+\.pov

// Ring distribution failing on the master is the expected outcome of the
// multi-arm transfer cancel and image storage-fault scenarios; the downstream
// arm reports the concrete per-arm failure which keeps the rule specific.
arm \d+: cmd: failed to distribute ring files
